Deputies took place."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d01", "start": 277, "end": 418, "text": "From the first meeting of the parliament, the Fontaine government had to face opposition from the liberals who described him as a \"turncoat\"."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d01", "start": 419, "end": 553, "text": "When Gaspard-Théodore-Ignace de la Fontaine received only a feeble majority in a confidence vote in the Chamber, he decided to resign."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d01", "start": 554, "end": 616, "text": "Jean-Jacques Madelaine Willmar, the son of the former governor"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d02", "start": 0, "end": 109, "text": "been charged with forming a new government after Wurth-Paquet, president of the Court, had refused this task."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d02", "start": 110, "end": 274, "text": "From 23 September 1854 additionally: The first task of the Simons government was to re-establish good relations with the governments of the Netherlands and Prussia."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d02", "start": 275, "end": 391, "text": "The treaty with the German customs union (Zollverein) was renewed shortly before its expiration on 26 December 1853."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d02", "start": 392, "end": 536, "text": "Charles-Mathias Simons restarted the negotiations on the Grand Duchy's participation in reimbursing the debts of the Kingdom of the Netherlands."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d02", "start": 537, "end": 631, "text": "In return, the Dutch crown guaranteed diplomatic protection for Luxembourgish subjects abroad."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d02", "start": 632, "end": 678, "text": "The resignation of the Willmar cabinet and its"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d03", "start": 0, "end": 324, "text": "shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia , the free encyclopedia Charles-Mathias Simons , Prime Minister 1853-1860 The Simons Ministry was in office in Luxembourg from 23 September 1853 to 26 September 1860 ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d03", "start": 325, "end": 441, "text": "Initially it just consisted of three members of the government , to which two more were added on 23 September 1854 ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d03", "start": 442, "end": 582, "text": "It was reshuffled on 24 June 1856 , and again on 2 June 1857 , when Paul de Scherff was placed in charge of railways , and Guillaume-Mathias"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d04", "start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "into force on 1 August 1848 ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d04", "start": 30, "end": 111, "text": "[ 1 ] On 28 September the first elections to the Chamber of Deputies took place ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d04", "start": 112, "end": 259, "text": "[ 1 ] From the first meeting of the parliament , the Fontaine government faced opposition from the liberals who described him as a `` turncoat '' ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d04", "start": 260, "end": 402, "text": "[ 1 ] When Gaspard-Théodore-Ignace de la Fontaine received only a feeble majority in a confidence vote in the Chamber , he decided to resign ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d04", "start": 403, "end": 520, "text": "[ 1 ] Jean-Jacques Madelaine Willmar , the son of the former governor of Luxembourg in the time of the United Kingdom"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d05", "start": 0, "end": 43, "text": "commission came to India in February 1928 ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d05", "start": 44, "end": 89, "text": "‘ Go back Simon ’ slogans were being raised ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d05", "start": 90, "end": 322, "text": "A new generation of youth got a channel to participate in political actions which also provided fertile ground for the spread of radical socialist ideas as was seen with the emergence of groups such as Punjab Naujawan Bharat Sabha ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d05", "start": 323, "end": 368, "text": "Nehru and Bose emerged as new youth leaders ."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d05", "start": 369, "end": 415, "text": "The protests were met with severe repression ."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d05", "start": 416, "end": 464, "text": "Senior leaders like- Jawahar Lal Nehru and G.B ."}, "D6S7": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d05", "start": 465, "end": 520, "text": "Pant and Lala Lajpat Rai in Lahore were lathi-charged ."}, "D6S8": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0458-2290b238a752:d05", "start": 521, "end": 563, "text": "Table of Contents Recommendations of Simon"}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["1 August 1848", "2 December 1848", "23 September 1853", "26 September 1860", "March 1848", "23 September 1854", "24 June 1856", "2 June 1857", "26 December 1853", "February 1928"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "1 August 1848", "origin": "coverage_addition"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "2 December 1848", "origin": "coverage_addition"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "23 September 1853", "origin": "coverage_addition"}, {"